L79: Figure 2a -  Levels of GSH (a) in liver homogenates 48h after the last session of the resistance training program in sham-operated sedentary (Sham-Sed), ovariectomized sedentary (Ovx-Sed), sham-operated resistance training, (Sham-Rt) and ovariectomized resistance training (Ovx-Rt). Values are presented as mean ± SDM;  p ≤ 0.05. a  statistically significant difference compared to Sham-Sed,  c  compared to Sham-Rt. Figure 2b -  Levels of GSSG (b) in liver homogenates 48h after the last session of the resistance training program in sham-operated sedentary (Sham-Sed), ovariectomized sedentary (Ovx-Sed), sham-operated resistance training, (Sham-Rt) and ovariectomized resistance training (Ovx-Rt). Values are presented as mean ± SDM;  p ≤ 0.05. a  statistically significant difference compared to Sham-Sed,  c  compared to Sham-Rt. Figure 2c -  Levels of GSH/GSSG (c) in liver homogenates 48h after the last session of the resistance training program in sham-operated sedentary (Sham-Sed), ovariectomized sedentary (Ovx-Sed), sham-operated resistance training, (Sham-Rt) and ovariectomized resistance training (Ovx-Rt). Values are presented as mean ± SDM;  p ≤ 0.05. a  statistically significant difference compared to Sham-Sed,  c  compared to Sham-Rt. Figure 2d -  mRNA expression of glutathione peroxidase (GSH-Px) in the liver 48 h after the last session of the resistance training program in sham-operated sedentary (Sham-Sed), ovariectomized sedentary (Ovx-Sed), sham-operated resistance training, (Sham-Rt) and ovariectomized resistance training (Ovx-Rt). Values are presented as mean ± SDM;  p ≤ 0.05. a  statistically significant difference compared to Sham-Sed,  b  compared to Ovx-Sed.
